# A file called SANITY_TOKEN.env sat here holding a Sanity token. It matched
# neither ".env" nor ".env.*" — those anchor at the START of the name, and this
# one only ENDS in .env. It was one `git add -A` away from a public repository.
# Suffix and substring, not just prefix.
*.env
!.env.example
*token*
*secret*
